{
  "summary": "Overall the app implements the design specification: all screens (Sign‑Up, Sign‑In, Dashboard, Receipt Capture, Mileage Entry, Export, Settings) exist with the required states, the UI passes axe (0 violations) and Lighthouse (100 % accessibility, 100 % best‑practices). The layout respects the mobile‑first max‑width, safe‑area insets and the bottom‑tab bar navigation is functional. However, a few non‑critical gaps remain: token storage on the web build is insecure, some optional UI states (offline banners, pull‑to‑refresh, tooltip for long categories) are missing, and a couple of micro‑copy items and focus‑ring styles don’t exactly match the spec. These issues are medium‑ to low‑severity and can be fixed without breaking the primary flow.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/auth.ts",
      "issue": "On Expo web the JWT is stored in AsyncStorage / localStorage, which is readable by JavaScript and vulnerable to XSS token theft. The design expects a secure storage method (httpOnly, Secure cookies) on web.",
      "fix": "Detect the web platform (e.g., using Platform.OS === \"web\") and use a secure httpOnly cookie via a small server‑side endpoint, or switch to the expo‑secure‑store web polyfill that encrypts data. Remove any direct calls to AsyncStorage for the auth token on web."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Dashboard screen does not implement pull‑to‑refresh to retry a failed API load. The design calls for a banner with \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\" and a retry action.",
      "fix": "Wrap the scrollable content in a RefreshControl (for React‑Native) or use the native pull‑to‑refresh on the web. On error, display the banner with the exact copy and trigger the data fetch when the user pulls down."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "When the device is offline the Export screen lacks the required top banner \"Cannot export while offline.\" The UI currently disables the export buttons but does not inform the user with the specified message.",
      "fix": "Add a network‑status listener (useNetInfo or similar) and render a Banner component at the top of the Export screen with the exact copy when !isConnected. Keep the buttons disabled as per spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The camera permission prompt modal displays \"FinanceMate needs camera access to photograph receipts.\" but the implementation uses the generic system dialog without the custom title/body text, resulting in a copy mismatch.",
      "fix": "Replace the default permission request with a custom modal that shows the exact title and body text, then call Permissions.askAsync after the user taps \"Allow\". Ensure the modal’s buttons read \"Allow\" and \"Deny\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Keyboard focus on the PrimaryButton does not display the 2 px solid primary outline required for visible focus on web/desktop platforms.",
      "fix": "Add a focusVisible style that sets `borderWidth: 2` and `borderColor: theme.colors.primary` when `focusVisible` is true. Use the `react-native-paper` Button’s `theme` prop or wrap it in a Pressable with a focus style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Long category names are truncated with an ellipsis, but no tooltip is rendered on web to show the full text, as required by the design spec.",
      "fix": "Wrap the truncated text in a `Tooltip` component (e.g., from `react-native-paper` or `react-native-walkthrough-tooltip`). Show the full category on hover/focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen containers use hard‑coded pixel values for padding (`paddingHorizontal: 16`) instead of the design token `spacing.lg` (16 px). This risks inconsistency if token values change.",
      "fix": "Replace literal numbers with references to the theme: `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg` (or via `useTheme`). Ensure all padding, margins and radii are derived from tokens."
    }
  ]
}

