{
  "summary": "Overall the app meets the primary flow and passes automated accessibility (axe 100 % and Lighthouse 100 % accessibility) and layout checks. However, several required design states, accessibility details, and security‑related UI practices are missing or incomplete. The most critical gaps are unimplemented error/offline states on Dashboard and Receipt Capture and insecure JWT storage on the web build. A number of medium‑severity issues (vulnerable npm packages, missing password‑visibility toggle, missing ARIA focus indicators, hard‑coded colors, missing autocomplete attributes) also need to be addressed before the product can be considered polished and production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Dashboard does not render the API error banner (\"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\") or the offline banner (\"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\") defined in DESIGN.md, leaving those states unhandled.",
      "fix": "Add conditional UI that displays a top Banner component when the fetch request fails (catch error) or when the NetInfo listener reports offline. Use the design token colors (`color-error` for error, `color-secondary` for offline) and ensure the banner respects safe‑area insets."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing the Permission Prompt modal (Allow/Deny) and the Permission Denied notice with \"Choose from library\" button, as required for the receipt‑capture flow.",
      "fix": "Wrap the camera request in a component that shows a `Dialog` (Paper) with the exact copy from DESIGN.md. If permission is denied, render a fallback notice view with the required button. Hook into `expo-image-picker` permission API to trigger these UI states."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Form does not display field‑level errors linked via `aria-describedby`, nor does it prevent submission when validation fails (submit button can be pressed while fields are invalid).",
      "fix": "Validate inputs on change, render `HelperText type=\"error\"` under each invalid field, set `accessibilityDescribedBy` on the TextInput, and disable the primary button (`disabled={hasErrors}`) until all fields are valid."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a show/hide toggle and autocomplete attributes; missing visible focus outline on the sign‑in button and input fields for keyboard navigation.",
      "fix": "Add a right‑icon button that toggles `secureTextEntry` and provides `accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"`. Set `autoComplete=\"email\"` on the email input and `autoComplete=\"current-password\"` on the password input. Ensure `PrimaryButton` includes a `focusVisibleStyle` with a 2 px solid `color-primary` outline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form field component does not expose a visible focus indicator (focus ring) and uses hard‑coded border colors instead of the design tokens (`primary` for focused, `error` for error). This violates the required interaction states and accessibility focus visibility.",
      "fix": "Update the component to use `theme.colors.primary` for the focused border, `theme.colors.error` for error state, and add a `focusVisibleStyle` with a 2 px solid `color-primary`. Pull all spacing, radius, and elevation from `theme`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button does not render a focus‑visible outline and uses a hard‑coded background color instead of the `primary` token; loading state spinner is missing in some screens.",
      "fix": "Wrap the Paper `Button` with `contentStyle` and `style` that reference `theme.colors.primary` and `theme.colors.onPrimary`. Add `focusVisibleStyle` with the required outline. Ensure `loading` prop displays a spinner next to the label."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen wrapper does not set `maxWidth: 360` or centre content, thereby potentially allowing side‑scroll on small devices, violating the mobile layout spec.",
      "fix": "Apply `style={{ paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg, maxWidth: 360, alignSelf: 'center', flex: 1 }}` to the root `View` or `SafeAreaView` and ensure parent containers respect this constraint."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/auth.ts",
      "issue": "JWT is stored in `AsyncStorage` (or localStorage on web) which is accessible to JavaScript and vulnerable to XSS token theft.",
      "fix": "Switch to `expo-secure-store` for native builds and for web use an `httpOnly` Secure cookie set by the backend (or a library like `js-cookie` with `secure` flag). Remove any direct usage of `AsyncStorage` for tokens on web."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/package-lock.json",
      "issue": "Vulnerable npm packages: `braces` 3.0.3 (DoS), `node‑forge` 1.4.0 (RSA signature forgery), `decode-uri-component` 0.2.2 (DoS), `uuid` 7.0.3 (out‑of‑bounds write), `sprintf-js` 1.0.3 (DoS).",
      "fix": "Upgrade or replace each library: move to a newer `braces` version once available, replace `node‑forge` with `@stablelib` or Web Crypto API, bump `decode-uri-component` to >=0.5.0, use `uuid` >=11.1.1, and replace `sprintf-js` with native template literals or a maintained alternative."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "EmptyState component uses a hard‑coded image path and does not reference the CSS custom property `--color-primary` for the CTA button, deviating from the token‑based styling rule.",
      "fix": "Replace any literal color values with `theme.colors.primary` or CSS variable `var(--color-primary)`. Use the component’s `PrimaryButton` which already consumes the token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export screen does not show a disabled state with spinner next to the CSV/PDF buttons while generation is in progress; the UI only shows a full‑screen spinner.",
      "fix": "Add button‑level disabled prop and a small `ActivityIndicator` inside the button label to match the design token `spacing.sm` and `color-primary` for spinner. Ensure the button label text remains visible."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline banner (\"Cannot export while offline.\") is not displayed when the device is offline, leaving that state unhandled.",
      "fix": "Listen to NetInfo state, and conditionally render a top `Banner` component with the exact copy from DESIGN.md when `!isConnected`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/ListItem.tsx",
      "issue": "ListItem does not provide `role=\"listitem\"` and does not set `accessibilityState={{ selected }}` for the pressed state, reducing semantic richness.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"listitem\"` and pass `accessibilityState` based on press/selection. Use the design token `spacing.md` for padding."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Settings icon button lacks an explicit `accessibilityLabel` and does not expose a focus‑visible outline.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Settings\"` and ensure the button's style includes the 2 px solid `color-primary` outline on focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "OpenAPI schema is publicly accessible at `/openapi.json`, potentially leaking endpoint details.",
      "fix": "Set `openapi_url=None` in the FastAPI constructor or protect the endpoint with authentication/IP restriction."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "Signup endpoint returns a specific error for existing email, enabling account enumeration.",
      "fix": "Return a generic success message regardless of account existence or unify error messages to avoid revealing the state."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "GET `/media/{filename}` endpoint has no rate‑limiting, allowing potential abuse.",
      "fix": "Add a `@limiter.limit(\"10/minute\")` decorator to the media endpoint or move media serving behind a CDN with signed URLs."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button does not include `aria-live` region for loading state announcements, which could affect screen‑reader feedback.",
      "fix": "When `loading` prop is true, set `aria-live=\"polite\"` on a hidden `Text` element with the loading message (e.g., \"Creating account…\")."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Long category text truncation tooltip for web is not implemented, missing the edge case defined in DESIGN.md.",
      "fix": "Wrap the category text in a component that conditionally renders a `Tooltip` (e.g., Paper's `Tooltip` or custom) when the text overflows, using `title` attribute for native browsers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen wrapper does not set `accessibilityRole=\"main\"` on the root container, missing a required landmark.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"main\"` to the top‑level `View`/`SafeAreaView` in each screen component."
    }
  ]
}

