{
  "summary": "The UI passes automated accessibility (axe) and best‑practice (Lighthouse) checks with perfect scores, but the primary user flow is broken: the \"Don’t have an account? Sign up\" link on the Sign‑In screen cannot be located or clicked in either mobile or desktop test runs. This prevents new users from reaching the Sign‑Up screen, halting the onboarding flow. No other critical accessibility violations were detected, but a review of the component code (not fully visible) suggests a lack of evidence that all design‑token‑driven styles, state variants, and required screen states (loading, error, empty) are implemented. Those omissions are noted as medium‑to‑low risk issues.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Don’t have an account? Sign up\" link is not present in the DOM or is not focusable/clickable, causing the primary flow from Sign‑In to Sign‑Up to time out during automated navigation tests.",
      "fix": "Add a Text/Button component for the link with the exact copy \"Don’t have an account? Sign up\", ensure it uses the PrimaryButton/TextLink wrapper which applies the design token colors and a visible focus ring, and wire it to the navigation stack (e.g., navigation.navigate('SignUp')). Also add an appropriate accessibilityRole=\"button\" and accessible label."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "There is no evidence that the PrimaryButton component defines all interaction states (default, hover, focus‑visible, pressed, disabled, loading) using the theme’s color tokens and that a 2 px solid primary focus ring is rendered.",
      "fix": "Extend the button wrapper to include style rules for each state using theme.colors.primary, theme.colors.primaryVariant, and theme.colors.disabled, and add a focus style (outline: 2px solid ${theme.colors.primary}) to meet the design spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen containers do not explicitly enforce the max‑content width of 360 px, horizontal padding, and safe‑area insets required for the mobile‑first layout.",
      "fix": "Apply the style { maxWidth: 360, alignSelf: 'center', paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg, flex: 1 } to every Screen wrapper, and ensure the SafeAreaView respects inset padding."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/theme.ts",
      "issue": "Design tokens for radii, spacing, and typography are defined, but the UI component code (e.g., FormField, SummaryCard, EmptyState) does not reference these tokens consistently; some hard‑coded values may be used.",
      "fix": "Audit each component’s style props and replace any literal numbers (e.g., margin: 16, borderRadius: 8) with theme.spacing.xxx and theme.roundness values."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Dashboard screen does not show the exact empty‑state copy \"You haven’t added any receipts or mileage yet. Tap the + button to get started.\" and the CTA \"Add first receipt\" as defined in the spec; default placeholders may be different.",
      "fix": "Implement the EmptyState component with the exact title, body, and CTA text from the spec, and link the CTA to the FAB action that opens the ReceiptCapture screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export screen lacks explicit disabling of the Export CSV/PDF buttons and spinner placement during the loading state as defined (buttons disabled + spinner next to button).",
      "fix": "Add loading state handling that disables both buttons, shows ActivityIndicator next to the appropriate button, and displays the spinner message \"Generating CSV…\" or \"Generating PDF…\"."
    }
  ]
}

