{
  "summary": "The UI layer passes the automated accessibility (axe), Lighthouse (100 % accessibility & best‑practices), and flow tests – all screens from the spec are present, the bottom tab bar is always reachable, and the design tokens are wired into the component library. Styling is applied (no orphan class names) and the layout respects the mobile‑first max‑content width and safe‑area insets. However, the codebase still carries critical security weaknesses that can break the primary user flow (DoS via regex, signature forgery, and insecure token storage on the web). These issues must be remedied before the product can be considered production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/package-lock.json",
      "issue": "Dependency `braces@3.0.3` contains CVE‑2026‑93687 (regular‑expression denial‑of‑service) with no patched version yet. An attacker could craft input that stalls the app, breaking the primary receipt‑capture flow.",
      "fix": "Replace the library with an alternative that does not rely on vulnerable regex processing (e.g., use native string methods) or upgrade to a fixed version as soon as it is released."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/package-lock.json",
      "issue": "Dependency `node‑forge@1.4.0` is vulnerable to CVE‑2026‑85393 (RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature forgery). This can be exploited to forge JWTs or other signatures, compromising authentication and breaking the login/sign‑up flow.",
      "fix": "Swap `node‑forge` for a maintained cryptography library such as `@stablelib` or the Web Crypto API, and remove all remaining references."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/auth.ts",
      "issue": "On Expo web builds the JWT is stored in AsyncStorage / localStorage, which is readable by any script and vulnerable to XSS token theft.",
      "fix": "For the web target store the token in an HttpOnly, Secure cookie set by the backend, or use a secure web‑compatible storage solution (e.g., `expo-secure-store` with a web fallback)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "Receipt image validation only checks MIME type and size; it does not limit image dimensions or pixel count, allowing a crafted decompression‑bomb image to consume excessive CPU/memory and cause a denial‑of‑service.",
      "fix": "Set `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS` to a safe threshold, enforce explicit width/height limits, and reject images that exceed them. Consider scanning uploads with an antivirus library."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "Authenticated media endpoint `/media/{filename}` lacks any rate‑limiting, so a valid user can flood the route and exhaust server resources.",
      "fix": "Apply a SlowAPI limiter (e.g., `@limiter.limit(\"10/minute\")`) to the endpoint or enforce rate limits at the edge/proxy."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "OpenAPI schema (`/openapi.json`) is publicly accessible, exposing endpoint signatures and model definitions.",
      "fix": "Set `openapi_url=None` in the FastAPI constructor for production, or protect the endpoint with authentication / IP‑based restrictions."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "Interactive API docs (`/docs`, `/redoc`) are exposed without authentication.",
      "fix": "Disable the docs in production (`docs_url=None`, `redoc_url=None`) or secure them behind auth."
    }
  ]
}

