{
  "summary": "The UI mostly follows the design spec and the primary flow works, but there are several accessibility and usability gaps that break compliance with the DESIGN.md. The most critical issue is a missing accessible name on image elements (role=\"img\" without alt), which makes parts of the app unusable for screen‑reader users. Additional medium‑severity gaps include missing autocomplete attributes, absent password‑show/hide and live‑validation UI, missing descriptive text on loading overlays, and missing focus‑visible styling. Minor token‑usage inconsistencies and performance concerns are also noted.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Image element rendered with role=\"img\" but no alt text or accessibilityLabel; Axe flagged a serious role‑img‑alt violation.",
      "fix": "Pass an explicit `accessibilityLabel` (or `alt` for web) prop to the image component, e.g., `<Image source={...} accessibilityLabel=\"No data illustration\" />`. If the image is purely decorative, set `aria-hidden=\"true\"` or `accessible={false}`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Receipt preview image in ReceiptCaptureScreen lacks an accessible label; screen readers will announce a generic \"image\" without context.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Receipt photo\"` (or `alt=\"Receipt photo\"` for web) to the preview image component. Ensure it is linked via `accessibilityRole=\"image\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading overlays (e.g., during account creation, receipt upload) display only a spinner, missing the mandated copy text like \"Creating account…\" or \"Uploading receipt…\". This leaves a state without the required copy and can confuse users.",
      "fix": "Extend the LoadingOverlay component to accept a `message` prop and render it beneath the spinner. Pass the exact strings defined in DESIGN.md for each loading state."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields do not include `autoComplete` attributes (e.g., `autoComplete=\"email\"` for email, `autoComplete=\"current-password\"` for login, `autoComplete=\"new-password\"` for sign‑up). This reduces usability and can increase security risk on shared devices.",
      "fix": "Prop‑gate `autoComplete` from the screen components to the underlying `TextInput`, using the appropriate HTML autocomplete values. For React‑Native Paper, set `textContentType` and `autoComplete` accordingly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a show/hide toggle and live validation UI for the 12‑character rule with uppercase, lowercase, number, and symbol. This violates sign‑up best‑practice requirements.",
      "fix": "Add an eye‑icon button inside the password `TextInput` (`right` prop) that toggles `secureTextEntry`. Implement a live‑validation component that displays each rule with a checkmark as the user types, using the `HelperText` component."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Interactive buttons do not have a visible focus ring on keyboard navigation (focus‑visible state). This fails the accessibility requirement for visible focus indicators.",
      "fix": "Add a style rule for `:focus-visible` (or RN's `onFocus` handling) that applies a 2 px solid `primary` outline. Ensure the same rule works in web via CSS and in native via the `style` prop."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline banner (\"You're offline – data may be outdated.\") defined in DESIGN.md is not implemented, leaving the offline state without a visible UI cue.",
      "fix": "Detect network status using `NetInfo` (React Native) or the `navigator.onLine` API (web) and conditionally render a banner at the top of the Dashboard with the exact copy and design token colors."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Card component uses hard‑coded background colors (`backgroundColor: '#FFFFFF'`) instead of the `surface` token from the theme, violating token consistency.",
      "fix": "Replace hard‑coded colors with `theme.colors.surface` (or use the Paper `Card` default theme) and ensure any custom styles reference token variables."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/web/theme.css",
      "issue": "Some components use raw pixel values for spacing (e.g., margin: 10px) that do not map to the 4/8 px design grid, causing potential layout drift.",
      "fix": "Audit CSS and replace ad‑hoc spacing with the CSS custom properties (`--space-xs`, `--space-sm`, etc.) to maintain the design grid."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "BottomTabBar tabs lack `accessibilityState={{ selected }}` and `accessibilityLabel` props for screen‑reader navigation, which reduces semantic clarity.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityState` and `accessibilityLabel` for each tab item, using the token colors for active/inactive states."
    }
  ]
}

