{
  "summary": "The Expo React‑Native UI largely follows the DESIGN.md specification and passes the automated Lighthouse/axe audits (accessibility 100, best‑practices 100). All screen files exist, the component wrappers use the design‑token theme, and the primary flow (sign‑up → dashboard → receipt/mileage capture → export) works on both phone and desktop. However, a few design‑driven details are missing or only partially implemented, which affect accessibility, completeness of required states, and best‑practice form handling. These issues are not fatal to the primary flow but should be fixed before production to ensure a polished, fully accessible product.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button components lack a visible focus indicator on web (no 2 px solid primary outline on keyboard focus), which violates the \"visible focus\" requirement and makes the app inaccessible for keyboard users.",
      "fix": "Add a `focusVisibleStyle` or CSS class that applies `outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary);` when the button receives focus. Ensure the style is included in the web stylesheet and that the React‑Native‑Paper `Button` receives the `style` prop for focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field does not provide a show/hide toggle (eye icon) nor `autocomplete=\"new-password\"`, breaking sign‑up best‑practice guidelines.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `TextInput` in a `FormField` with a right‑hand `IconButton` that toggles `secureTextEntry`. Add `autoComplete=\"new-password\"` prop to the password input. Update the component documentation and ensure the toggle updates the field visibility without losing focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Email and password inputs lack `autocomplete` attributes (`email` and `current-password`) and are missing appropriate `autoCapitalize`/`autoCorrect` settings, which degrades form usability and accessibility.",
      "fix": "Add `autoComplete=\"email\"` to the email field and `autoComplete=\"current-password\"` to the password field. Set `autoCapitalize=\"none\"` and `autoCorrect={false}` on both fields to match native expectations."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The offline banner (`\"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\"`) defined in the spec is not rendered when the app detects loss of connectivity, leaving the offline state unhandled.",
      "fix": "Implement a `useNetInfo` hook (or similar) to monitor network status and display a `Banner` component at the top of the dashboard with the exact copy when `isConnected` is false. Ensure the banner is dismissible with a clear ARIA role (`alert`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The permission‑denied notice does not include the exact copy \"Choose from library\" button and the modal text does not match the required phrasing, resulting in a mismatch with the design spec.",
      "fix": "Update the permission‑denied UI to show a `PrimaryButton` labelled \"Choose from library\" that triggers the image‑picker fallback. Ensure the modal title and body use the exact strings from the spec (`\"Camera access needed\"` and `\"Allow FinanceMate to use your camera so you can photograph receipts.\"`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Inline field‑error messages are not linked to their inputs via `aria-describedby`, so screen readers may not announce the error associated with a field.",
      "fix": "When rendering `HelperText` for an error, generate a unique ID (e.g., `${fieldId}-error`) and set `accessibilityDescribedBy={errorId}` on the `TextInput`. Ensure the `HelperText` component includes `id={errorId}`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The placeholder illustration in the empty‑state does not have an `accessibilityLabel` or `accessible={false}` declaration, causing screen readers to treat the decorative image as content.",
      "fix": "Add `accessible={false}` to the Image component or provide an empty `accessibilityLabel=\"\"` to mark it as decorative. Verify that the surrounding text elements have proper heading roles."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The `Screen` wrapper uses a hard‑coded `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg` but does not respect safe‑area insets on iOS (e.g., notch, home indicator).",
      "fix": "Wrap the content in a `SafeAreaView` with `edges={['bottom', 'left', 'right']}` and merge its padding with the theme spacing to ensure content does not overlap device cutouts."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "The overlay spinner is rendered with a plain `View` that lacks an ARIA role of `status` or `alertdialog`, so assistive technologies may not announce loading states.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"status\"` and `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"` to the overlay container, and ensure the spinner has an accessible label (e.g., `\"Loading…\"`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons display a loading spinner but do not disable the opposite button, allowing simultaneous CSV and PDF generation contrary to the spec which says the other button should be disabled while one is loading.",
      "fix": "When one export action is in progress, set `disabled={true}` on the other button. Track export state in component state (`loadingExport: 'csv' | 'pdf' | null`) and conditionally disable the non‑active button."
    }
  ]
}

