{
  "summary": "The FinanceMate UI largely fulfills the DESIGN.md spec – all screens and states are reachable, axe reports zero accessibility violations, Lighthouse scores 100 % for accessibility & best‑practices, and the primary flow was validated on both phone and desktop. However, a few design‑consistency and security details are missing: some components still use hard‑coded colors/sizes instead of the design tokens, the Sign‑Up/Sign‑In forms omit autocomplete attributes and a password‑show/hide toggle, a handful of user‑visible copy strings deviate from the exact wording in the spec, and the front‑end relies on high‑severity vulnerable npm packages and stores the JWT in plain AsyncStorage on the web build. These issues don’t break the core flow but should be fixed before a production release.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields lack `autoComplete` props (email and password) and the password field has no show/hide toggle, which violates the sign‑up best‑practice guidelines.",
      "fix": "Add `autoComplete=\"email\"` to the email TextInput and `autoComplete=\"new-password\"` to the password TextInput. Implement a right‑icon button that toggles `secureTextEntry` and updates its accessibility label (\"Show password\" / \"Hide password\")."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same as Sign‑Up: missing autocomplete attributes and missing password show/hide control, also the password live‑rule helper is not rendered.",
      "fix": "Add `autoComplete=\"username\"` (or \"email\") and `autoComplete=\"current-password\"` to the respective TextInputs, implement a toggle icon, and render the live‑rule helper text below the password field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button styling uses hard‑coded colors (`#0066FF`, `#FF9800`) and border radius values instead of the design‑token values from `theme.ts`.",
      "fix": "Replace inline color values with `theme.colors.primary` / `theme.colors.accent` and use `theme.roundness` for border radius. Ensure the button’s `contentStyle` pulls spacing from `theme.spacing`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Card background and elevation are hard‑coded (`backgroundColor: '#FFF'`, `shadowOpacity: 0.2`) rather than using `theme.colors.surface` and `theme.elevation.card`.",
      "fix": "Bind the component’s style to `theme.colors.surface` and spread `theme.elevation.card` for shadows. Remove any magic numbers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The wrapper does not enforce the max‑content width of 360 px or respect safe‑area insets on iOS/Android; layout occasionally overflows on small devices.",
      "fix": "Add `maxWidth: 360`, `alignSelf: 'center'`, and `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg`. Wrap the root view in `SafeAreaView` and set `flex: 1` to respect insets."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No explicit focus‑visible outline is defined; on web the button receives focus but the required 2 px solid `primary` outline is missing.",
      "fix": "Add a `focusStyle` or `style` that applies `borderWidth: 2`, `borderColor: theme.colors.primary` when `focused` state is true (use the `onFocus`/`onBlur` callbacks)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Error toast message for submission failure displays \"We couldn’t create your account…\" whereas the spec expects the exact text \"We couldn’t create your account. Please check the fields and try again.\" (missing period).",
      "fix": "Update the toast content to match the spec exactly, including punctuation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/package.json",
      "issue": "High‑severity vulnerable dependencies (`braces`, `node-forge`, `decode-uri-component`, `uuid`, `sprintf-js`) are still present in the lockfile.",
      "fix": "Upgrade to patched versions where available or replace the libraries (e.g., swap `node-forge` with `@stablelib` or Web Crypto API, replace `sprintf-js` with template literals). Run `npm audit fix` and verify no remaining CVE‑affected packages."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/auth.ts",
      "issue": "JWT token is stored in AsyncStorage/localStorage for the web build, which is vulnerable to XSS token theft.",
      "fix": "Switch to httpOnly, Secure cookies for the web target (e.g., using `expo-secure-store` with web fallback that writes a SameSite=Strict cookie) or a library that abstracts secure storage across platforms."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "API error messages (e.g., \"Email already registered\") do not match the user‑facing copy defined in DESIGN.md, which can lead to mismatched toast text.",
      "fix": "Map backend error details to generic messages as defined in the spec (e.g., always return \"We couldn’t create your account…\" for signup failures)."
    }
  ]
}

