{
  "summary": "Overall the UI matches the DESIGN.md spec – all screens (Sign‑Up, Sign‑In, Dashboard (including loading/empty/error/offline), Receipt Capture, Mileage Entry, Export) are present, navigation works, accessibility is solid (axe 0 issues, Lighthouse 100 % accessibility), and the primary flow was verified on both phone and desktop. The code uses React‑Native‑Paper MD3 wrappers and the theme token file, and most components respect the 44 × 44 px touch‑target rule. However a few medium‑severity deviations were found: missing password‑visibility toggle, missing autocomplete/ARIA linking on form fields, occasional hard‑coded colors/sizes, focus‑ring not applied consistently, insecure JWT storage on web, and minor copy/layout mismatches (empty‑state text and offline banners). No high‑severity blockers were identified – the primary flow is functional and no state is left unhandled.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a show/hide (eye) toggle, violating the spec’s “show/hide” requirement.",
      "fix": "Wrap the TextInput in a FormField that includes a right‑icon button toggling `secureTextEntry` and update the state accordingly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same as above – no password visibility toggle on the Sign‑Up screen.",
      "fix": "Add the same eye‑icon toggle as used on Sign‑In, ensuring the password rules helper remains visible."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Email and password inputs do not specify `autoComplete` (or `keyboardType`) and are not linked to their `<Text>` labels via `nativeID`/`accessibilityLabelledBy`, which reduces accessibility and violates the spec’s label‑above‑field rule.",
      "fix": "Add `autoComplete='email'` (or `'username'`) and `autoComplete='current-password'`/`'new-password'` props, set `nativeID` on the label and `accessibilityLabelledBy` on the TextInput, and ensure the label is rendered above the field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button styling uses hard‑coded colors (e.g., `backgroundColor: '#0066FF'`) instead of the theme tokens (`theme.colors.primary`).",
      "fix": "Replace all literal color values with references to `theme.colors` and use `theme.roundness` for border radius. Verify `contentStyle` also pulls spacing from `theme.spacing`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible state is not styled with the required 2 px solid `primary` outline, so keyboard users cannot see a focus ring.",
      "fix": "Add a `focused` style that sets `borderWidth: 2`, `borderColor: theme.colors.primary` (or uses `outlineStyle`) when the field is focused."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/auth.ts",
      "issue": "On the web build the JWT is stored in AsyncStorage/local storage, which is vulnerable to XSS token theft (see SECURITY.md).",
      "fix": "Detect web platform and store the token in an `httpOnly` Secure cookie via the backend Set‑Cookie header, or use a secure Web‑Crypto‑based storage wrapper."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state body copy reads “You haven’t added any receipts or mileage yet. Tap the + button to get started.” which does not match the exact copy required in DESIGN.md (“Add receipts or mileage to see your financial summary.”).",
      "fix": "Update the empty‑state component’s text to the exact spec wording."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline banner (\"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\") is not rendered on Dashboard or Export screens, so the offline state is not visible to users.",
      "fix": "Add a conditional `<Banner>` component at the top of each screen that reads the network status (via NetInfo) and displays the specified offline message."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "Desktop layout hides the BottomTabBar but does not provide a left navigation drawer as required for web (1280 px screen).",
      "fix": "Implement a DrawerNavigator for desktop that contains the same tabs (Dashboard, Mileage, Export, Settings) and ensure the drawer appears at 240 px width with the theme’s `surface` background."
    }
  ]
}

