  "summary": "The UI is generally structured with the promised screens and wrapper components, but a critical navigation failure (Sign‑In → Sign‑Up) prevents the primary onboarding flow. Several design‑system and accessibility best‑practices are missing or only partially implemented: loading states/disabled fields on auth forms, autocomplete and secure‑text toggles on password inputs, proper ARIA roles and focus outlines for navigation elements, and occasional hard‑coded style values that bypass the MD3 design tokens. These gaps will cause users to encounter dead‑ends, reduced usability on keyboards and screen‑readers, and visual inconsistencies on mobile and web.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Don’t have an account? Sign up\" link is rendered as plain text (or a non‑Pressable component) and cannot be clicked. Automated flow test timed out trying to navigate to the Sign‑Up screen.",
      "fix": "Replace the link with a Pressable/TouchableOpacity or Paper Button that has an onPress handler navigating to the Sign‑Up route. Add `accessibilityRole=\"link\"` and ensure it is focusable (keyboard Tab) and has a visible focus outline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "During account creation the UI does not disable the input fields or show the overlay spinner described in the Loading state. The button remains enabled, allowing duplicate submissions.",
      "fix": "Wrap the form in a LoadingOverlay component and set `disabled` on FormField components when the submit promise is pending. Show the spinner and replace button label with \"Creating account…\" as defined in the spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The sign‑in form similarly lacks field‑level loading/disable behaviour and does not display the \"Signing you in…\" overlay spinner.",
      "fix": "Implement the same LoadingOverlay pattern as Sign‑Up and toggle `disabled` on the email/password fields while the login request is in flight."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "TextInput components are missing `autoComplete` / `textContentType` props (e.g., email, password) and therefore do not trigger native autofill on iOS/Android. Password fields also lack a show/hide toggle and live validation feedback.",
      "fix": "Pass `autoComplete=\"email\"` and `textContentType=\"emailAddress\"` for email fields, and `autoComplete=\"current-password\"` / `textContentType=\"password\"` for password fields. Add a trailing eye‑icon button that toggles `secureTextEntry` and expose an accessible label (\"Show password\" / \"Hide password\"). Wire the live password rule list to display validation errors as the user types."
