{
  "summary": "All automated headless audits (axe, Lighthouse, layout) report zero accessibility violations and the primary flow works flawlessly on both mobile and desktop. However, a manual UI review uncovered several divergences from the DESIGN.md specifications and best‑practice UI patterns. The most notable gaps are missing password‑visibility toggles and autocomplete attributes on the auth forms, inconsistent use of design tokens (hard‑coded colors, sizes, and spacing), lack of a visible focus ring on interactive elements for keyboard users, missing alt text on decorative images, and a few components that still use inline values instead of the theme. None of these issues break the primary flow, but they affect visual fidelity, usability, and strict adherence to the design system.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password input does not include a show/hide toggle and is missing autocomplete=\"new-password\", violating the sign‑up best‑practice checklist.",
      "fix": "Add a trailing eye icon button that toggles secureTextEntry and set autocomplete=\"new-password\" on the TextInput. Also link the label via nativeID for accessibility."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password input lacks a show/hide toggle and autocomplete=\"current-password\", and the email field lacks autocomplete=\"email\".",
      "fix": "Add the eye icon toggle for password visibility, set appropriate autocomplete attributes for email and password, and ensure labels are correctly associated."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Error state uses hard‑coded color #D32F2F and border width instead of the theme’s colors.error and spacing tokens, breaking the token‑only style rule.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded color with theme.colors.error and use theme.spacing.sm for border thickness. Ensure all states (focused, error, disabled) reference theme values."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No explicit focus‑visible style is defined; on web the button shows the default browser outline, which does not match the required 2 px solid primary outline.",
      "fix": "Add a style rule for :focus-visible that sets border: 2px solid ${theme.colors.primary} and removes the default outline. Use React Native Paper’s `theme` to apply the same on native platforms."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "Icon size is hard‑coded to 26 px and label font size to 14 px, deviating from the spec’s 24 px icons and 12 px caption.",
      "fix": "Reference theme.spacing.lg for icon size (24 px) and theme.typography.labelSmall for label font size. Remove any inline numeric values."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The illustration Image component lacks an accessibilityLabel or alt text, making it invisible to screen readers.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Empty state illustration\"` (or mark `accessible={false}` if decorative) and ensure the Image respects the accessibility props."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Preview thumbnail image does not have an `accessibilityLabel` or `role=\"img\"`, and the surrounding View is not marked as an image container.",
      "fix": "Wrap the thumbnail in a component that sets `accessibilityLabel=\"Receipt photo preview\"` and `accessibilityRole=\"image\"`. Also ensure the image is not announced as decorative."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Overlay background uses a hard‑coded RGBA value (#00000080) rather than a token from the theme (e.g., colors.disabledBackground with opacity).",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded overlay color with a token-derived color, e.g., `${theme.colors.disabledBackground}80` or a semantically named overlay token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Drawer navigation items are plain TouchableOpacity elements without `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` or `accessibilityState` indicating selected, which reduces screen‑reader clarity.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` and `accessibilityState={{ selected: isActive }}` to each drawer item, and ensure the label is readable."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Layout uses inline padding values (e.g., paddingHorizontal: 16) instead of the design token `spacing.lg` (16 px), causing inconsistency when token values change.",
      "fix": "Replace all hard‑coded padding and margin numbers with the corresponding `theme.spacing` values. Verify that the maxWidth is applied via the token (`spacing.xxl` for 360 px)."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "score": 5,
  "summary": "Basic sign-in screen with functional elements, but lacks visual polish and design consistency. The layout is minimal and unstyled, resembling browser defaults, with no grid alignment, no spacing hierarchy, and no brand identity. The primary action is clear but the overall presentation feels crude and unprofessional for a polished product.",
