{
  "summary": "The app loads, passes axe and Lighthouse, and the primary flow works, but several design‑system and accessibility gaps remain that break the spec or degrade the user experience. These gaps include missing interaction states (focus outlines, hover/pressed colors), incomplete sign‑up/in forms (no password show/hide toggle, no live rule list, missing autocomplete attributes, submit button can be silently disabled), missing empty‑state copy in the Dashboard, missing error‑toast copy for some API failures, missing persistent navigation on the web drawer, and some design‑token misuse (hard‑coded colors/sizes in a few components). Because these issues prevent the product from meeting the spec’s “no forward path missing” and accessibility requirements, they are flagged as high severity.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑up form lacks a password visibility toggle, live validation rule list, and autocomplete attributes; also the submit button becomes disabled without a visible loading indicator, violating sign‑up best practices and the specified copy.",
      "fix": "Add a show/hide eye icon button with proper `accessibilityLabel` and `accessibilityState` to toggle `secureTextEntry`. Render the live rule list under the password field and link it to the input via `aria‑describedby`. Set `autoComplete=\"email\"` and `autoComplete=\"new-password\"`. Ensure the \"Create account\" button shows a loading spinner with the text \"Creating account…\" and is not silently disabled."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑in form also misses the password show/hide toggle, autocomplete attributes, and focus‑visible outlines; the loading state does not display the exact \"Signing you in…\" message.",
      "fix": "Implement the same password visibility toggle as sign‑up, add `autoComplete=\"email\"` and `autoComplete=\"current-password\"`, render a loading overlay with the spinner and the text \"Signing you in…\", and ensure all focusable elements have a 2 px solid `primary` outline on focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty state on the Dashboard uses placeholder text instead of the exact copy \"You haven’t added any receipts or mileage yet. Tap the + button to get started.\" and the CTA button label does not match \"Add first receipt\". Also the offline banner copy is missing.",
      "fix": "Update the EmptyState component to display the exact title \"No data yet\", body copy as specified, and a PrimaryButton labelled \"Add first receipt\". Add a Banner component that shows \"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\" when the app detects offline status, using the correct token colors."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button styling uses hard‑coded hex colors and dimensions instead of the `theme.colors.primary` and `theme.spacing` tokens, breaking the design‑token contract.",
      "fix": "Replace all inline color values with `theme.colors.primary`/`theme.colors.primaryVariant` etc., and use `theme.spacing.lg` for padding, `theme.roundness` for border radius. Ensure the `minHeight` is 48 px and `minWidth` is 120 px as defined."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Cards use a hard‑coded shadow style instead of the `elevation.card` token and have a static width that can cause horizontal scrolling on narrow phones (<390 px).",
      "fix": "Apply `...theme.elevation.card` for elevation, set `maxWidth: 360` and `marginHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg` to respect global max‑content width, and verify no overflow occurs."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Root `<View>` does not have `accessibilityRole=\"main\"` and lacks proper safe‑area handling; on devices with notches the bottom tab bar can be overlapped.",
      "fix": "Wrap the content in a `<SafeAreaView accessibilityRole=\"main\">` and apply `paddingBottom: theme.spacing.lg` to avoid overlap with the FAB and tab bar."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Permission prompt modal does not include the exact copy \"FinanceMate needs camera access to photograph receipts.\" and the fallback “Choose from library” button label differs. Also missing error toast copy for upload failures.",
      "fix": "Update the permission modal text to match the spec, ensure the fallback button is labeled exactly \"Choose from library\", and standardize toast messages to use \"Upload failed. Check your connection and try again.\" as defined."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing loading overlay with the exact \"Saving mileage…\" message and missing error toast copy \"Failed to save mileage. Please try again.\". Also the Save button can be disabled without a visible spinner.",
      "fix": "Render a full‑screen overlay with a spinner and the text \"Saving mileage…\" during the API call. Show the error toast with the exact copy on failure. Keep the Save button enabled with a loading state indicator."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons lack disabled state styling and do not show a spinner next to the CSV/PDF button with the exact \"Generating CSV…\" / \"Generating PDF…\" messages. Toast after share does not use the specified copy.",
      "fix": "When export starts, disable both buttons, show a spinner next to the active button, and display a temporary banner with the required message. After sharing, show a toast \"Report ready to share.\""
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "On web, the left drawer navigation is hidden and the bottom tab bar remains visible, violating the spec that the drawer should provide navigation and the bottom tab bar should be hidden on desktop.",
      "fix": "Add a breakpoint that hides `<BottomNavigation>` when viewport width >= 1280 px and renders `<Drawer>` with the same navigation items. Ensure the drawer respects the 240 px width and uses the `surface` token for background."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The EmptyState component does not include a visible focus outline for the CTA button when navigated via keyboard, nor does it expose a proper `role=\"alertdialog\"` for screen readers.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"alertdialog\"` to the container and ensure the CTA button receives the standard focus outline (2 px solid `primary`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields lack the required `nativeID` + `accessibilityLabel` linking, and the error `HelperText` is not associated via `accessibilityDescribedBy`, breaking the accessible error indication pattern.",
      "fix": "Generate a unique `nativeID` for each TextInput, set the corresponding label’s `htmlFor` (or `accessibilityLabel`), and pass the error ID to `HelperText` via `accessibilityDescribedBy`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "Tab items do not expose `role=\"tab\"` and `aria‑selected` (or `accessibilityState={{ selected }}`) attributes, and the focus ring on tabs is missing, violating keyboard navigation and visible focus requirements.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"tab\"` and `accessibilityState={{ selected }}` to each tab button, and apply a 2 px solid `primary` outline when focused."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Toast.tsx",
      "issue": "Toast component does not call `announceForAccessibility` on mount, so screen readers do not announce success or error messages, contrary to the accessibility spec.",
      "fix": "Import `announceForAccessibility` from `react-native` and invoke it with the toast message when the component mounts."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Some screens contain unused CSS class names (e.g., `container`, `wrapper`) without corresponding style rules, indicating styling is not applied as intended.",
      "fix": "Remove unused class names or create matching style definitions using the Design Tokens. Verify with the style audit that `unmatchedCount` remains 0."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "Media endpoint does not enforce rate‑limiting on per‑user basis and returns raw files without `Cache‑Control` headers, risking DoS and leaking data. While not a UI issue, it violates the spec’s security expectations for forward navigation and data protection.",
      "fix": "Add a per‑user rate limit (e.g., `@limiter.limit(\"5/minute\")`) and set appropriate `Cache-Control: private, max‑age=0` headers on `FileResponse`."
    }
  ]
}

